Wat je gaat doen As a MIG/MAG Welder, you’ll contribute to the production of high-quality trailers. 

Your responsibilities include:- Welding: performing MIG/MAG welding on structural components according to technical drawings and specifications;
- Assembling: building components into complete trailers;
- Maintaining: keeping your workspace clean and organized and ensuring proper maintenance of tools;
- Inspecting: checking weld seams and assemblies for quality and accurate dimensions;
- Improving: contributing ideas for more efficient working methods within the production process;

   Wat we je bieden You’ll have the opportunity to use your craftsmanship in an innovative and collaborative working environment.

 We offer:- A gross monthly salary of €3.250 to €3.500, based on 40 hours per week;
- A temporary contract with the prospect of a permanent position;
- A full-time 40-hour workweek, from 07:30 to 16:15;
- 38 days off per year: 25 vacation days + 13 ADV days;
- €0.23 net travel allowance per kilometer for distances over 10 km;
- A modern workplace with advanced technology and an informal working atmosphere;
- Opportunities to further develop your skills and technical knowledge;
- A good work-life balance within a collegial working environment.

   Functie-eisen We’re looking for a precise and team-oriented MIG/MAG Welder with a passion for craftsmanship and an eye for detail.- Proven experience with MIG/MAG welding and reading technical drawings;
- Available for full-time day shifts from 07:30 to 16:15;
- Good command of Dutch, German or English, both spoken and written;
- A collaborative and collegial attitude;
- Willingness to learn and openness to new techniques;
- MBO 4 work and thinking level, preferably in a production-related field;
- A practical welding test at the company is part of the application process.

